https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z4xHzqV3Ctw  (Capo 0)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and (FaddG) and add the 5th note as needed).

TIP:  The key to playing the (CaddG) (FaddG) sequence, which emulates the banjo, is to keep your index finger planted on the 2nd string/1st fret and pinky planted on the 1st string/3rd fret.   They never move off these frets and there's no reason to barre the 1st string on the 1st fret to cover the <f> part of the (FaddG) since it's removed from play by the pinky on the 3rd fret.  Just shift your ring and middle fingers down one string for the (FaddG) and then back up for the (CaddG).  Then you can leave the pinky on the 1st string/3rd fret for the next (G).  This sequence is in the intro, and begins the song, but also notice it repeats after "Old Joe's Place" so when you see it coming come off the (G) in front of "Old" get ready to include the pinky on the 1st string of the (CaddG) for "place."

TIP:  The (Cmaj7) can be skipped if you prefer as it's just a pretty inconsequential transistion chord.

TIP:  For the “Pick it” there are two options and notice they all begin with a series of chords strums and a final single strum of |G|, followed by two quick strums of |G|-|C|.  The first is to play the part with individual chord strums.  Line two are individual notes (notes may or may not transpose).  It says "pick it" so you might as well pick it!  All the notes are on the bottom two strings and frets 1 and 3.  It's a simple little walk up/down.  So off the strum of |G| immediately go to the 2nd string/1st fret <c>.  Practice it first before playing the song.  Sweet!}
       
    
